<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>		     28/11/96		 21/11/96	     1/12/95</p>
<p>    Gasoline	400-425			450		   350</p>
<p>    Naphtha	   50-75		   75-100		   100</p>
<p>    Gas oil   2,000-2,050		    2,100	 1,800-1,825</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	325-350			375		   400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     25			 25		    10</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks dipped as some cargoes moved out of the area, although product movements still centred on the record IPE delivery, material mainly being barged direct to storage.</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks fell with no incoming cargoes, but barges left, mainly to Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories also dipped as product left to Germany.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks were down as little product arrived, but some did leave bound for Germany and the bunker market.</p>
<p>Jet fuel arrived, but was swiftly blended into the gas oil pool.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
